atch the new behavior; no narrative/ladder edits, no CAD touched.\n\n## Runtime evidence\n\n`runtime/lifecycle/posters-policy-parent/report.json` (parent run, 23:47–23:51Z): V4 pass — reduced-motion-static desktop+narrow: `requests: []`, `glbRequests: []`, probe `status: \"ready\"`; poster cases additionally show `glCanvasCount: 0`, `threeScene: null`. Source tests 445/43 and build 703 PASS per spec.\n\n## Limitations\n\nThe reduced-motion cases record no canvas-absence observables (`glCanvasCount`/`threeScene` exist only in poster cases), so \"no connected WebGL canvas for fresh reduced startup\" is code-inferred plus zero-request evidence, not directly observed — browser acceptance pending on that observables gap. V6 remains pending. The latest opening full-tier failure is untouched by this change and stays unresolved. This is a GLM review; it cannot claim a Fable verdict.\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
